type SystemAdminDashboardSummary {
    totalSchools: Int!
    activeSchools: Int!
    inactiveSchools: Int!
    pendingRegistrations: Int!
    """
    How many calendar days (Vietnam time) the OLDEST application has been waiting in the queue.

    null when no application is waiting any more — very different from 0, which means "there is an application, just submitted today". Here 0
    is the best state, so mixing the two up would draw an empty queue that looks exactly like a
    queue that was just cleared.
    """
    oldestPendingRegistrationDays: Int
    registrationsLast30Days: Int!
    registrationsLast90Days: Int!
    totalRevenue: Float!
    "Revenue of the last 24 months, ordered oldest to newest"
    monthlyRevenue: [MonthlySpending!]!
    studentCount: Int!
    teacherCount: Int!
    schoolAdminCount: Int!
    activeFrameworkCount: Int!
    systemRubricCount: Int!
}

type MonthlySpending {
    "Format YYYY-MM"
    month: String!
    amount: Float!
}

type SchoolMonthlySpending {
    "Format YYYY-MM"
    month: String!
    amount: Float!
    "Spend on plan subscription/renewal"
    subscriptionAmount: Float!
    "Spend on buying extra tokens"
    tokenTopUpAmount: Float!
}

type SubscriptionRenewal {
    planName: String
    status: SchoolSubscriptionStatus!
    "End of the current subscription period"
    endDate: DateTime!
}

"""
The school's money, at a level that is enough to answer "can we still run assessments this week".

MONEY IN THIS TYPE IS String, not Float -- deliberately deviating from the general convention of the file, because the wallet balance is
numeric(18,6) and a double rounds wrongly exactly where the number has to match absolutely. The full reason is at the top of
school-balance.graphqls. All four fields use the same type: mixing Float with String in the same money
block is harder to read than being inconsistent with tokenAllocated/tokenUsed right next to it.

TWO DIFFERENT POCKETS, do not merge them: the plan quota is split by QuotaType (only the ASSESSMENT wallet pays for assessment
grading), while the self-topped-up wallet is ONE shared number and is only deducted when the quota of the corresponding kind is exhausted.
A roomy speaking-practice pocket does not help next week's assessment.
"""
type SchoolFunding {
    "REMAINING grading quota. Never negative — any excess has become debt on the wallet."
    assessmentQuotaRemainingVnd: String!
    assessmentQuotaTotalVnd: String!
    "Self-top-up wallet balance. Negative IS the debt."
    balanceVnd: String!
    """
    balanceVnd < 0 — the school cannot open new exam sessions.

    The same rule SchoolSubscriptionDebtGuardService uses to block VerifyAssessmentScheduleOtpUseCase and
    StartClassTestSessionUseCase, returned ready-made instead of making the client compare with 0: a rule should be defined in only one place.
    Deliberately has the same meaning as SchoolBalance.locked — this is the companion read for the overview page.
    """
    locked: Boolean!
    """
    assessmentQuotaRemainingVnd + max(balanceVnd, 0). A NEGATIVE wallet is not subtracted here: the debt is an amount owed.

    Does NOT subtract committedToUsersVnd. This is the LOCK predicate — matches ClassTestTokenQuotaGuardService.spendableSchoolFundsVnd
    to the last dong, the real gate that refuses to schedule an exam.
    Subtracting the promised part here would report that money has run out while the system still allows spending.
    """
    spendableVnd: String!
    """
    The part already promised to teachers through personal spending ceilings that they have NOT spent. Never negative.

    It adds the UNSPENT part, not the total allocated: what a teacher has already spent is already in
    assessmentQuotaRemainingVnd (ConsumeQuotaService deducts the same dong from both the school wallet and the personal
    counter), so taking the total allocated would subtract twice. A row that has spent beyond its ceiling contributes 0, not a
    negative number -- going over the ceiling is money really spent, not a credit handed back to the school.

    ASSESSMENT wallet only. The student's ceiling lives in the PRACTICE wallet and pays nothing for assessment grading.
    """
    committedToUsersVnd: String!
    """
    spendableVnd - committedToUsersVnd — how much the school can still spend freely on CENTRALIZED exams without
    eating into the part promised to teachers.

    NEGATIVE is an answer, not an error: the school has allotted more to teachers than the money remaining.
    DistributeQuotaToUsersService caps the total allocation by pool.totalAllocated × ratio, i.e. by the TOTAL
    and not by the REMAINING part, so this state is reachable without anyone doing anything wrong. Consequence:
    the last person to spend is refused by the school wallet even though their personal ceiling still has room — exactly the situation that
    ClassTestTokenQuotaGuardService.computeSharedPoolInsight warns about when scheduling a centralized exam.
    """
    uncommittedVnd: String!
}

"""
Submissions whose exam is finished but the student has NO score yet, split by what is blocking them.

The five groups are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE and cover everything — they add up to exactly `total`.

NOT taken from gradingStats.unassigned even though it sounds similar: that counts submissions ELIGIBLE for one more grading
round, a set that includes RELEASED / INVALID / APPEALED, i.e. almost every submission of the school.

The scope is CENTRALIZED exams whose scores are NOT yet published. Exams already RESULTS_PUBLISHED are excluded because both AI re-grading
and reassigning the grader are refused there — those submissions are no longer work to do but
damage already done, and leaving them here would give the number a floor that never returns to 0.
"""
type UnscoredWorkload {
    total: Int!
    "aiFailedRetryLeft + aiFailedNoRetryLeft — the UI merges them into one row, the two sub-numbers are secondary labels"
    aiFailed: Int!
    "AI grading failed, nobody has touched it, and the school still has AI re-grade attempts left"
    aiFailedRetryLeft: Int!
    "AI grading failed, AI attempts used up — only manual grading remains"
    aiFailedNoRetryLeft: Int!
    "Already in the grader queue but not yet assigned to anyone"
    awaitingAssignment: Int!
    assignedOverdue: Int!
    assignedInProgress: Int!
    "How many calendar days (VN time) the longest-waiting submission has waited; null when no submission is left — null is DIFFERENT from 0"
    oldestWaitingDays: Int
    assessmentCount: Int!
}

"""
Exams that are CLOSED but still have submissions without a score.

Publishing scores is a ONE-WAY door: RetryGradingAssessmentSessionUseCase and HandOffGradingToHumanUseCase
both refuse when the exam is in RESULTS_PUBLISHED. Clicking publish while blank submissions remain permanently closes the books on
exactly those submissions, and no screen currently warns about it beforehand.

Only CLOSED exams — exactly the set of exams where the Publish scores button can be clicked. IN_PROGRESS exams still have people sitting the exam,
so blank submissions are normal there.
"""
type AssessmentAwaitingPublish {
    assessmentId: ID!
    code: String!
    name: String!
    "null for an assessment with no close time"
    closeAt: DateTime
    unscoredCount: Int!
    "Of those, still recoverable with AI"
    aiFailedRetryLeft: Int!
    "Of those, AI attempts used up — a teacher must be assigned to grade"
    aiFailedNoRetryLeft: Int!
    "Of those, already sitting in the grader queue"
    awaitingHumanGrading: Int!
}

"""
An attempt whose AI grading failed that nobody has handled yet, seen from the school's side.

NO score: a GRADING_FAILED session never produced an assessment_candidate_results row. What replaces it are the
fields that help choose between the two exits -- ask the AI to regrade, or assign a teacher to grade by hand.
"""
type SchoolGradingFailure {
    sessionId: ID!
    assessmentId: ID!
    assessmentCode: String!
    assessmentName: String!
    candidateName: String
    "null when the student has not been placed in any active class"
    className: String
    "Submission time"
    failedAt: DateTime
    "Raw error message, verbatim; null for a session marked failed through the DLT branch"
    error: String
    """
    How many times the grading service RETRIED by itself within one attempt; null when unknown.

    Entirely DIFFERENT from the school's quota: this number is about how persistent the incident is, not about who pressed what. Do not
    build buttons from it — schoolRetryLeft is what decides.
    """
    aiRetryCount: Int
    "Whether the school still has AI re-grade attempts for this session"
    schoolRetryLeft: Boolean!
}

type SchoolGradingFailurePage {
    content: [SchoolGradingFailure!]!
    page: Int!
    size: Int!
    totalElements: Int!
    totalPages: Int!
    """
    Number of submissions with AI attempts left, with the exam filter ALREADY applied but the quota filter NOT yet applied.

    These two numbers sit on the filter buttons themselves so they must predict the result of the click exactly. With no exam filter
    they match unscored.aiFailedRetryLeft / aiFailedNoRetryLeft on the overview page exactly.
    """
    retryLeftCount: Int!
    noRetryLeftCount: Int!
}

type SchoolAdminDashboardSummary {
    assessmentStatusCounts: AssessmentStatusCounts!
    appealStats: AppealStats!
    revenue: Float!
    "Spend of the last 12 months, ordered oldest to newest"
    monthlySpending: [SchoolMonthlySpending!]!
    """
    The ASSESSMENT GRADING quota of the running subscription period -- the ASSESSMENT wallet only, not including the speaking practice wallet.

    The field name says "token" and does not say "assessment" -- that is legacy; see SchoolFunding for the clearer reading, which
    also includes the wallet balance. The two places read the same quota record so they never diverge.
    """
    tokenAllocated: Float!
    tokenUsed: Float!
    "null if the school has never had an active subscription"
    subscriptionRenewal: SubscriptionRenewal
    funding: SchoolFunding!
    unscored: UnscoredWorkload!
    "Most blank submissions first. Cut at 5 exams — this is a warning card, not an exam list."
    assessmentsAwaitingPublish: [AssessmentAwaitingPublish!]!
    """
    How many calendar days (VN time) the longest-waiting PENDING complaint has waited.

    null when no complaint is waiting any more — very different from 0, which means "there is a complaint, just submitted today". Same lesson
    as oldestPendingRegistrationDays: the number of COMPLAINTS does not tell whether any complaint is late.
    """
    oldestPendingAppealDays: Int
}

type TeacherGradingStats {
    pending: Int!
    completed: Int!
}

type TeacherScoreStats {
    averageScore: Float
    gradedCount: Int!
    totalCandidates: Int!
}

type ClassScoreStats {
    assessmentName: String!
    className: String!
    averageScore: Float
    highestScore: Float
    lowestScore: Float
    gradedCount: Int!
    totalCandidates: Int!
}

type TeacherDashboardSummary {
    assessmentStatusCounts: AssessmentStatusCounts!
    gradingStats: TeacherGradingStats!
    scoreStats: TeacherScoreStats!
    classScoreStats: [ClassScoreStats!]!
}

type NearestCentralizedAssessment {
    assessmentId: ID!
    code: String!
    name: String!
    status: AssessmentStatus!
    "When the assessment opens"
    openAt: DateTime
    "When the assessment closes"
    closeAt: DateTime
    totalCandidates: Int!
    absentCandidates: Int!
}

type QuestionBankStats {
    totalQuestions: Int!
    totalQuestionBanks: Int!
    draft: Int!
    submittedForReview: Int!
    revisionRequested: Int!
    approved: Int!
    rejected: Int!
    published: Int!
    archived: Int!
    readAloud: Int!
    shortAnswer: Int!
    longAnswer: Int!
    opinion: Int!
    description: Int!
}

"AI grading results of one calendar day in Vietnam time."
type GradingOutcomeBucket {
    "Calendar day in Vietnam time"
    day: Date!
    graded: Int!
    failed: Int!
}

"""
Operational health of the platform. Mixes two kinds of time ON PURPOSE:

sessionsInProgress / assessmentsInProgress / gradingQueueDepth are a snapshot AT THE MOMENT OF THE CALL and do not change with
dateFrom/dateTo — "6 exams running now" changing when you click to the previous month would be meaningless. The remaining
fields belong to the window being viewed.
"""
type PlatformOperationalHealth {
    "Sessions in progress right now"
    sessionsInProgress: Int!
    "Number of DISTINCT exams that have a running session"
    assessmentsInProgress: Int!
    "Sessions that are submitted, queued or being graded"
    gradingQueueDepth: Int!
    "Sessions finished grading within the window"
    graded: Int!
    "AI-failed sessions within the window (assessment_sessions.status = GRADING_FAILED)"
    gradingFailed: Int!
    "null when the window has no session that finished grading or failed grading — very different from 0%"
    successRatePercent: Float
    "Continuous by day, old -> new, a day without sessions returns 0"
    daily: [GradingOutcomeBucket!]!
}

"""
Business health of the platform.

Every count is classified by SCHOOL, not by subscription row — a school has many periods in its history.
"In force" includes CANCELLED because that status only turns off auto-renewal, the school can still use the service until
endDate; only SUSPENDED loses access immediately.

DO NOT ADD THE COUNTS UP — they are not a partition:

* subscribedSchools / lapsedSchools / suspendedSchools are mutually exclusive: they are the three states that the
    same school can have at the time of the call.
* expiringSoonSchools is a SUBSET of subscribedSchools, not a fourth group.
* schoolsInDebt cuts across all three: it reads from school_balances and not from school_subscriptions, so
    a school that still has a plan but a negative wallet is counted in BOTH subscribedSchools and schoolsInDebt.
* Schools that have NEVER had any plan are not in the first three groups: they have no row in
    school_subscriptions to group. A newly approved school that has not bought a plan is therefore invisible here.

School counts are a snapshot AT THE MOMENT OF THE CALL, not changing with dateFrom/dateTo. The money figures follow the window
being viewed.
"""
type PlatformBusinessHealth {
    "Schools with a subscription period covering today"
    subscribedSchools: Int!
    "Subset of subscribedSchools: the covering period will end within the next 30 days"
    expiringSoonSchools: Int!
    "Once had a plan but no period covers now, and not suspended"
    lapsedSchools: Int!
    "Suspended and no period covers now"
    suspendedSchools: Int!
    "Negative self-top-up wallet — exactly the schools blocked from opening exam sessions"
    schoolsInDebt: Int!
    "Money actually received in the window (SUCCESS orders), VND"
    revenueVnd: Float!
    "Same length, immediately BEFORE the window — not the previous calendar month"
    previousRevenueVnd: Float!
    "AI cost price incurred in the window, VND (ai_usage_records.cost_vnd)"
    aiCostVnd: Float!
    "null when the window collected no money at all — a margin on 0 revenue does not exist, it is not 0%"
    grossMarginPercent: Float
    """
    Same formula, computed on the comparison period — to draw the difference in PERCENTAGE POINTS (not %).

    Computed on the server instead of letting the client subtract two ratios itself: the convention "if revenue is 0 the margin
    does not exist" is only correct if applied once to both periods. null when the previous period collected no money at all,
    and then there is NO difference to display.
    """
    previousGrossMarginPercent: Float
}

"""
A group of failed grading sessions with the same cause.

`signature` is the normalized error message (uuids and numbers replaced with blanks) — it is the IDENTIFIER of the
group, passed back unchanged into `gradingFailureSessions` to open the group. null is the "unknown
cause" group: a session marked failed through the DLT branch carries no message, and every session that failed before
the system started storing reasons is also here. It is a REAL group, not missing data.
"""
type GradingFailureGroup {
    signature: String
    "A representative raw error message, for reading; null in the unknown-cause group"
    sampleError: String
    sessionCount: Int!
    "System-level exams belong to no school so they are not counted"
    schoolCount: Int!
    assessmentCount: Int!
    "Together with lastFailedAt this shows whether the failures were an incident contained in two hours or a slow-burning error lasting two weeks"
    firstFailedAt: DateTime
    lastFailedAt: DateTime
    "Number of sessions in exams whose scores are NOT yet published, i.e. really re-gradable"
    retryableCount: Int!
}

"""
Page that classifies failed grading sessions.

sessionCount must match `gradingFailed` of platformOperationalHealth exactly when both use the same range:
same predicate (status = GRADING_FAILED), same window on submitted_at, same default when the bounds are omitted.
"""
type GradingFailureOverview {
    sessionCount: Int!
    "Number of cause groups, including the unknown-cause group if present"
    causeCount: Int!
    schoolCount: Int!
    retryableCount: Int!
    "Largest group first"
    groups: [GradingFailureGroup!]!
    """
    Number of groups over the cap that were cut from `groups`.

    Said out loud instead of cutting silently, because it is a DIAGNOSTIC SIGNAL: if message normalization fails to merge,
    the number of groups grows close to the number of sessions, and then the normalization needs fixing, not the cap raising.
    """
    groupsTruncated: Int!
}

"""
A failed grading session. NO score: a GRADING_FAILED session has no assessment_candidate_results row to
take a score from. What replaces it are the fields that help triage.
"""
type GradingFailureSession {
    sessionId: ID!
    schoolId: ID
    "null for a system-level exam"
    schoolName: String
    schoolCode: String
    assessmentId: ID!
    assessmentName: String!
    candidateName: String
    "Submission time"
    failedAt: DateTime
    "How many times the grading service tried before giving up; null when unknown"
    retryCount: Int
    "Raw error message, verbatim; null in the unknown-cause group"
    error: String
    "Exam whose scores are not published, i.e. re-gradable"
    retryable: Boolean!
    """
    Submission HAS been pushed to the grader queue.

    The session stays in GRADING_FAILED because the hand-off deliberately does not change the session status (see
    HandOffGradingToHumanUseCase), so this flag is the ONLY thing that tells a session that has someone assigned apart from a
    session nobody has touched.
    """
    handedOff: Boolean!
}

type GradingFailureSessionPage {
    content: [GradingFailureSession!]!
    page: Int!
    size: Int!
    totalElements: Int!
    totalPages: Int!
}

"""
Four groups of "schools needing attention". NOT a partition — do not add the four numbers up:

* EXPIRING_SOON is a SUBSET of the group of schools that still have a plan.
* LAPSED and SUSPENDED are mutually exclusive and exclusive of the group that still has a plan.
* IN_DEBT CUTS ACROSS all three: it reads from the wallet balance and not from the subscription status.

Schools that have NEVER bought any plan do not belong to the first three groups — they have no row in
school_subscriptions to group. This is exactly the same behavior as the count on the overview page, kept on
purpose so that the two screens say the same number.
"""
enum SchoolRiskBucket {
    EXPIRING_SOON
    LAPSED
    SUSPENDED
    IN_DEBT
}

type SchoolAtRisk {
    schoolId: ID!
    schoolName: String!
    schoolCode: String!
    "Name of the plan of the period RELATED to the group: the covering period if a plan remains, otherwise the most recent period"
    planName: String
    "End of that same period"
    relevantEndDate: DateTime
    "Most recent suspension reason; only meaningful in the SUSPENDED group"
    suspendedReason: String
    "Self-top-up wallet balance, VND. Negative means the school is blocked from opening exam sessions. Never null"
    balanceVnd: Float!
}

type SchoolAtRiskPage {
    content: [SchoolAtRisk!]!
    page: Int!
    size: Int!
    totalElements: Int!
    totalPages: Int!
}

"""
Counts of all four groups.

Taken from the SAME count that platformBusinessHealth uses, not recounted with another query — otherwise the
card on the overview page says 5, the user clicks it, and this screen shows 9.
"""
type SchoolRiskBucketCounts {
    expiringSoon: Int!
    lapsed: Int!
    suspended: Int!
    inDebt: Int!
}

type SchoolsAtRisk {
    bucket: SchoolRiskBucket!
    counts: SchoolRiskBucketCounts!
    schools: SchoolAtRiskPage!
}

"Grouping unit of the AI cost chart."
enum AiCostGranularity {
    DAY
    WEEK
    MONTH
}

"""
AI cost of a school over time.

MONEY is a String, not a Float — the source is numeric(18,6), same reason as stated at the top of
school-balance.graphqls.

Read from school_ai_spend_entries: the amount the SCHOOL IS CHARGED, not the platform's cost price. Those two numbers deliberately
differ since V9 (the cost of failed grading attempts is waived), so drawing this chart from ai_usage_records would
charge the school even the money we decided not to collect.

Fully replaces `schoolTokenUsageTimeseries` — that field never existed in the schema even though clients still
called it, and the only repository serving it summed `tokens_consumed` on a table no code has written to
since V2.
"""
type SchoolAiCostTimeseries {
    granularity: AiCostGranularity!
    "Total of exactly the points below — summed from the same set, not a second SUM query"
    totalCostVnd: String!
    points: [AiCostPoint!]!
    """
    The point at which the ledger starts having data; null when the school has never spent any money.

    V10 deliberately does NOT backfill (numbers rebuilt from ai_usage_records would differ from what was really charged), so every range
    before this point draws a flat line at 0 even if the school did spend money. The UI must be able to tell the difference
    between "spent nothing" and "not yet recorded".
    """
    recordedFrom: DateTime
}

type AiCostPoint {
    "Start of the bucket in Vietnam time -- date_trunc runs on the business zone, not on UTC"
    bucket: DateTime!
    quotaType: QuotaType!
    costVnd: String!
}

type UserAiSpend {
    userId: ID!
    fullName: String
    quotaType: QuotaType!
    spentVnd: String!
    "Personal spending ceiling; null when the school has not set a ceiling for this person — they can still spend, there is just no level to compare against"
    allocatedAmountVnd: String
}

"""
Who has spent how much of the school's AI quota in the window being viewed.

A person who spends from both wallet types gets TWO rows — one per type, because the spending ceiling is also divided by type.
"""
type SchoolAiSpendByUserPage {
    content: [UserAiSpend!]!
    page: Int!
    size: Int!
    totalElements: Int!
    totalPages: Int!
    """
    Spend that does NOT belong to anyone's ceiling — the part of centralized exams.

    Centralized exams are organized by the school, so they are deliberately not counted against any individual's pocket
    (CompleteAssessmentSessionGradingUseCase only passes the author for class tests). Returned separately
    instead of as an "unknown" row: in almost every school this is the LARGEST item and would take the top of
    the table, hiding exactly what this table exists to show.

    Summing the user rows and comparing against the chart will always be short by exactly this number.
    """
    schoolWideCostVnd: String!
}

extend type Query {
    systemAdminDashboard: SystemAdminDashboardSummary!

    """
    AI cost of the CURRENTLY LOGGED-IN school over time.

    It takes no schoolId -- the old version did, which meant a school admin who sent another school's id could read
    that school's spending.

    dateFrom is INCLUSIVE, dateTo is EXCLUSIVE. An omitted dateTo means the time of the call; an omitted dateFrom means
    30 days back.
    """
    schoolAiCostTimeseries(
        dateFrom: DateTime
        dateTo: DateTime
        granularity: AiCostGranularity! = DAY
    ): SchoolAiCostTimeseries!

    """
    Who is spending the school's AI quota. Same window convention and same defaults as
    `schoolAiCostTimeseries` -- the two blocks sit side by side, so they must read the same range.

    An omitted quotaType means both wallet kinds. Biggest spender first.
    """
    schoolAiSpendByUser(
        dateFrom: DateTime
        dateTo: DateTime
        quotaType: QuotaType
        page: Int = 1
        size: Int = 20
    ): SchoolAiSpendByUserPage!

    """
    List of schools in ONE attention group, with the counts of all four groups.

    Do NOT use `schoolSubscriptions` for this even though it also filters by status: that screen filters by
    subscription ROW while here we count by SCHOOL. A school whose 2024 period has ended and whose 2025 period is running would
    be in the status=EXPIRED list of that screen but does NOT belong to the LAPSED group.
    """
    schoolsAtRisk(
        bucket: SchoolRiskBucket!
        keyword: String
        page: Int = 1
        size: Int = 20
    ): SchoolsAtRisk!

    """
    Same range convention as platformOperationalHealth, and the same defaults: an omitted dateTo means now, an omitted
    dateFrom means 14 days back. A user who clicks the failed-session number on the overview expects to see exactly the
    sessions that produced that number.
    """
    gradingFailureOverview(dateFrom: DateTime, dateTo: DateTime): GradingFailureOverview!

    """
    Sessions of ONE group. `signature` is taken verbatim from GradingFailureGroup.signature -- omitting it
    or passing null selects exactly the "unknown cause" group, it does NOT drop the filter.
    """
    gradingFailureSessions(
        dateFrom: DateTime
        dateTo: DateTime
        signature: String
        page: Int = 1
        size: Int = 20
    ): GradingFailureSessionPage!

    """
    dateFrom is INCLUSIVE, dateTo is EXCLUSIVE -- two adjacent ranges would count a session on the exact boundary twice if
    <= were used, the same convention as schoolBalanceSummary. An omitted dateTo means now; an omitted dateFrom means
    14 days back.
    """
    platformOperationalHealth(dateFrom: DateTime, dateTo: DateTime): PlatformOperationalHealth!

    """
    Same range convention as platformOperationalHealth. An omitted dateFrom means the start of the current month in
    Vietnam time.
    """
    platformBusinessHealth(dateFrom: DateTime, dateTo: DateTime): PlatformBusinessHealth!

    """
    AI-failed submissions that NOBODY has handled yet, for the logged-in school — the landing place of the row of the same name on
    the overview page.

    Runs on exactly the set that `schoolAdminDashboard.unscored.aiFailed` counts: the same CTE produces both,
    so clicking the number 14 gives exactly 14 rows.

    Takes NO schoolId — the scope comes from the logged-in user.

    Omitting `retryLeft` means NO filter; true only takes submissions with AI re-grade attempts left, false only takes submissions
    with attempts used up. The two groups lead to entirely different actions so being able to separate them is worthwhile.

    Ordered OLDEST FIRST, the opposite of gradingFailureSessions for the system admin: that one asks "what just broke",
    this one asks "which student has waited longest and still has no score".
    """
    schoolGradingFailures(
        assessmentId: ID
        retryLeft: Boolean
        page: Int = 1
        size: Int = 20
    ): SchoolGradingFailurePage!

    schoolAdminDashboard: SchoolAdminDashboardSummary!
    teacherDashboard: TeacherDashboardSummary!
    "The centralized exam closest to the present time for the school — null if the school has no centralized exam yet"
    nearestCentralizedAssessment: NearestCentralizedAssessment
    questionBankStats: QuestionBankStats!
}
